This extension lets you change history. The core idea that I care about is that you can have a development branch and a review branch.

You can make all your changes in the development branch. The commit history shows the order in which these changes were made essentially providing you with local checkpoints.

Once you are ready to go for review, the reviewers may not care about this history. They would rather care for the change to be split into smaller parts either by functionality or file.

In the review branch:
(1) so now you graft the changes from dev to rev. Collapse them using histedit into a single change

(2) next use hg split to split this change into multiple changes as you see fit (for easy of review)

That's it.

--------
When review comments appear, you hg up to the change that added the piece of code being modified. Make the change, hg amend then hg evolve.

hg amend will cause the same change to be COW'ed, hg evolve will fix the ancestry. Send it out for review and continue this cycle for as long as it takes to get the change in.

--------
In Parallel you can continue development in the dev branch. If you want to pull the Review changes in, you must use hg graft for the review change that was modified. (hg amend
will create a separate change so the graft will go through) Do merge resolutions as needed.


That's it!! You keep the review branch for review and the dev branch for development and marching ahead if you must.

